From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: pwm: add allwinner,sun60i-a733-pwm

A new file rather than an enum entry in allwinner,because
the block it describes is not that block. In pwm-sun4i's register file 0x00 is
the control register and 0x04 is channel 0's period; on the A733 those two are
the interrupt enable and interrupt status registers (A733 UM V0.92 18.7.7,
A733 user manual). Nothing about the sun4i binding's shape carries over --
not the offsets, not the one-or-two-clock model, not "#pwm-cells = 3" meaning
the same fields against the same hardware.

Three clocks, and the split is real hardware rather than a driver convenience.
"bus" is the PWMn_BGR gate, needed to reach the registers at all. "hosc" and
"apb" are the two sources the block's own clock mux selects between in
PCCR.CLK_SRC (00 = SYS_CLK24M, 01 = APB0), so both have
to be named phandles: the driver picks one per channel pair and needs to know
each one's rate.

⚠ "hosc" is the SYS_CLK24M net, fixed at 24 MHz, NOT the 26 MHz
DCXO -- on this SoC those are two different nets and confusing them has produced
three separate defects in this tree. The binding cannot enforce it; the SoC
device tree is where it has to be right.

"resets" is required. PWMn_BGR bit 16 comes out of reset asserted, so a node
without it describes a controller that cannot run.

Two things left out on purpose. The always-on S_PWM instance at 0x07023000 has
the same register file but a different set of clock sources (DCXO / RTC_32K /
RC16M / SYS_CLK24M), which means a different CLK_SRC
encoding that has not been read here -- so it gets no compatible in this file
rather than a guessed one. And "interrupts" is optional: the block has one
(PWM0 = INTID 67 = GIC SPI 35, PWM1 = INTID 68 = GIC SPI 36, from
the interrupt list of the A733 user manual), it is real, and the driver added
alongside this binding does not use it -- capture is not implemented.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/pwm/allwinner,sun60i-a733-pwm.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/pwm/allwinner,sun60i-a733-pwm.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Allwinner A733 PWM
+
+maintainers:
+  - DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
+
+description: >
+  The A733 (sun60iw2) carries two of these controllers on the main bus, PWM0 at
+  0x02527000 and PWM1 at 0x02528000, with ten channels each. The register file
+  is not the one drivers/pwm/pwm-sun4i.c drives: offsets 0x00 and 0x04 are the
+  interrupt enable and status registers, channel output enable lives in PER at
+  0x80, and the per-channel registers start at 0x100 with a stride of 0x40.
+
+  The block also exists in the always-on domain as S_PWM at 0x07023000. That
+  instance takes a different set of clock sources and is not covered by this
+  binding.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: allwinner,sun60i-a733-pwm
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  clocks:
+    items:
+      - description: Bus clock, the controller's PWMn_BGR gate
+      - description: SYS_CLK24M, the 24 MHz source selectable in PCCR
+      - description: APB0, the other source selectable in PCCR
+
+  clock-names:
+    items:
+      - const: bus
+      - const: hosc
+      - const: apb
+
+  resets:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  "#pwm-cells":
+    const: 3
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - clocks
+  - clock-names
+  - resets
+
+allOf:
+  - $ref: pwm.yaml#
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/reset/sun60i-a733-ccu.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
+
+    pwm@2528000 {
+        compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-pwm";
+        reg = <0x02528000 0x400>;
+        interrupts = <GIC_SPI 36 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+        clocks = <&ccu CLK_BUS_PWM1>, <&osc24M>, <&ccu CLK_APB0>;
+        clock-names = "bus", "hosc", "apb";
+        resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_PWM1>;
+        #pwm-cells = <3>;
+    };
+
+...
